#### Mei Wen Chin (Centific Technologies Inc) [MSFT] on 9/18/2026, 00:44 PM: 

<p>Thanks for your sharing the detail steps, I can reproduce this issue through your shared steps and this issue has been escalated for further investigation, if there is any process, I will inform you immediately.</p>

**Version Used**: 

[56e8233a425fd97e32fccf0e1d3cc880d206e2e1](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/commit/56e8233a425fd97e32fccf0e1d3cc880d206e2e1)

**Steps to Reproduce**:

Compile the following code
```csharp
#nullable enable
namespace System.Runtime.CompilerServices
{
  public class UnionAttribute : System.Attribute
  {
  }
}

[System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Union]
struct S1 : S1.IUnionMembers
{
  public object? Value => throw null!;
  public bool HasValue => throw null!;
  public bool TryGetValue(out int x) => throw null!;
  public bool TryGetValue(out string? x) => throw null!;

  public interface IUnionMembers
  {
    object? Value { get; } 
    bool TryGetValue(out int x);
    bool TryGetValue(out string? x);

    static S1 Create(int x) => throw null!;
    static S1 Create(string x) => throw null!;
  }
}

class Program
{
  public void Test1(S1 s)
  {
    if (s.TryGetValue(out string value))
    {
      s.Value.ToString(); // warning
      value.ToString(); // warning
    }
  }

  public void Test2(S1.IUnionMembers s)
  {
    if (s.TryGetValue(out string? value))
    {
      s.Value.ToString(); // warning
      value.ToString(); // warning
    }
  }
}
```

**Diagnostic Id**:

`CS8602`

**Expected Behavior**:
Roslyn recognizes that after `TryGetValue` call on a uninon type returned `true`, according to the [union proposal](https://github.com/dotnet/csharplang/blob/main/proposals/csharp-15.0/unions.md#trygetvalue-and-nullable-analysis):
> When the non-boxing access pattern's HasValue or TryGetValue(...) are used to query the contents of a union type (explicitly or via pattern matching), it impacts Value's nullability state in the same way as if Value had been checked directly: The null state of Value becomes "not null" on the true branch.

**Actual Behavior**:
No `TryGetValue` check on a union with `IUnionMembers` interface updates neither `.Value` property state nor the state of the out argument.

**Notes**:
It looks like the checks at [NullableWalker.isUnionTryGetValueValue](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/blob/d382e078f7345ecf4f3cb51561f8dd20f652adb9/src/Compilers/CSharp/Portable/FlowAnalysis/NullableWalker.cs#L8569) and [NamedTypeSymbol.IsUnionTypeTryGetValueMethod](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/blob/d382e078f7345ecf4f3cb51561f8dd20f652adb9/src/Compilers/CSharp/Portable/Symbols/NamedTypeSymbol.cs#L2862) contradict each other so no call can satisfy both.

`NullableWalker` requires a union receiver type, which an interface cannot satisfy
`NamedTypeSymbol` requires that whenever a member provider interface exists the method definition should come from it

An invocation on a union member interface can't satisfy the `NullableWalker` check
An invocation on a union type itself can't satisfy the `NamedTypeSymbol` check
So the non-boxing access pattern cannot be used with the member providers at all without false positive nullability warnings
